{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "SNG",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair;Thine eyes are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doves behind thy veil.\nThy hair is as a flock of goats,\nThat lie along the side of mount Gilead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy teeth are like a flock ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of ewes",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "newly",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shorn,\nWhich are come up from the washing,Whereof every one hath twins,\nAnd none is bereaved among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy lips are like a thread of scarlet,\nAnd thy mouth is comely.\nThy temples are like a piece of a pomegranate\nBehind thy veil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy neck is like the tower of David\nBuilded for an armory,\nWhereon there hang a thousand bucklers,\nAll the shields of the mighty men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy two breasts are like two fawns\nThat are twins of a roe,\nWhich feed among the lilies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Until the day be cool, and the shadows flee away,\nI will get me to the mountain of myrrh,\nAnd to the hill of frankincense.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art all fair, my love;\nAnd there is no spot in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come with me from Lebanon, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bride,\nWith me from Lebanon:Look from the top of Amana,\nFrom the top of Senir and Hermon,\nFrom the lions’ dens,\nFrom the mountains of the leopards.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bride;\nThou hast ravished my heart with one of thine eyes,\nWith one chain of thy neck.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How fair is thy love, my sister, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bride!\nHow much better is thy love than wine!\nAnd the fragrance of thine oils than all manner of spices!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy lips, O ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bride, drop ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the honeycomb:\nHoney and milk are under thy tongue;\nAnd the smell of thy garments is like the smell of Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A garden shut up is my sister, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bride;\nA spring shut up, a fountain sealed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy shoots are an orchard of pomegranates, with precious fruits;\nHenna with spikenard plants,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Spikenard and saffron,\nCalamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense;\nMyrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a fountain of gardens,\nA well of living waters,\nAnd flowing streams from Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Awake, O north wind; and come, thou south;\nBlow upon my garden, that the spices thereof may flow out.\nLet my beloved come into his garden,\nAnd eat his precious fruits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
